From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:01:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/38] fs: sharedfs: file data through the window with DAX

Regular files are DAX inodes. read, write, mmap and exec go through the
kernel's DAX code against a window the host maps 2 MiB chunks of files
into on request (MAP), so the guest's view of a file is the host page
cache itself: a host write is visible to the next guest read with no
message, and a guest write lands in the host's page cache directly. The
page-cache copy path (OPEN, RELEASE, READ, read_folio) is gone.

data.rs keeps the chunk table (slot and chunk index to window offset),
hands extents to DAX through the iomap operations, counts users per
chunk, and when the window is full reclaims the least recently used idle
chunk: break its layout, UNMAP it, reuse the offset. A fault path never
reclaims; it reports EAGAIN and the fault handler retries. An inode
gives its chunks back when it is destroyed. A write past the end of the
file has the host EXTEND it first. A host-side shrink drops the guest's
mappings beyond the new size.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
